<http://data.silknow.org/object/b3a832ba-6851-3522-ab0b-ef5aee21f4a7>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Half of a man's wrapped garment, complete piece probably intended to be joined to another. Red and yellow checked cotton field, with end and border stripes in red, white, orange, black and yellow silk. One side border with chevron designs; two end borders with green horizontal band and black, white and red narrow guard bands."@en , "Textile, part of a man's wrapped garment, cotton and silk, Tatta, ca. 1854"@en , "The complete piece would have been intended for use as a garment, clothing."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/7236bfb0-9d8d-3979-8c5f-b0351e1449c1> ;
